one pallas_call, grid=(N,) (one image per step, "arbitrary"); the whole net stays in VMEM as planar
(C, rows, lanes) f32 buffers with 8 zero rows on top and zero lanes past the width (NCHW needs no transpose).
3x3 convs = VPU FMAs over row strips (~4-8 vregs per accumulator) with scalar SMEM weights and pltpu.roll taps;
relu+maxpool fused (strided row loads, lane-pair max, MXU 0/1 compaction); nearest resize = 0/1 matmuls;
conv after an x2 upsample runs sub-pixel (4 parity 2x2 convs: 2.25x fewer FMAs), interleaved by MXU + strided stores.
outside the kernel: only weight astype/reshape/concat and a final slice of the lane/row-padded bf16 output.

